<!--meta {"lead": "Buttons let people act: send a request, find braiders, cancel an appointment. One primary button per view tells them which action matters most.", "description": "Five variants, three sizes, icon and block forms, every state in both themes.", "pills": ["Native <code>&lt;button&gt;</code>", "Status: stable"], "variants": "primary, secondary, ghost, link, danger; leading/trailing icon; icon-only; block", "states": "default, hover, focus, active, disabled, loading, pressed", "sources": ["pages/booking-request/default", "pages/appointment-detail/default", "dialogs/cancel-appointment/default", "pages/booking-request/submitting"]} -->
<section class="ds-section" id="overview"><h2><a href="#overview">Overview</a></h2>
  <p>Use a button when activating it changes something: it submits, sends, cancels, opens a dialog or starts a process. Use a <a href="link.html">link</a> when it only takes the person somewhere; a link that looks like a button (<code>&lt;a class="btn"&gt;</code>) is still a link. Use a <a href="menu.html">menu</a> when one trigger offers several actions.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Primary</b> is the one action the view exists for: "Send request", "See braiders for this style", "Post review". Never two per view.</li>
    <li><b>Secondary</b> (the default look) is every other action: "Find braiders", "Request a change", "Keep browsing".</li>
    <li><b>Ghost</b> sits inside dense surfaces: the dialog close button, toolbar and row actions.</li>
    <li><b>Link</b> looks like a link but is a low-emphasis action beside other buttons: "Cancel request" on the appointment card.</li>
    <li><b>Danger</b> is for destructive confirmations and appears only inside a confirmation dialog: "Cancel request", "Sign out".</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="anatomy"><h2><a href="#anatomy">Anatomy</a></h2>
  <div class="ds-anatomy">
    <figure class="ds-anatomy__figure">
      <button class="btn btn--primary btn--lg" type="button">{{icon:calendar}}Request with Nia</button>
      <span class="ds-callout" style="left: 31%; top: 22%;" aria-hidden="true">1</span>
      <span class="ds-callout" style="left: 52%; top: 22%;" aria-hidden="true">2</span>
      <span class="ds-callout" style="left: 72%; top: 72%;" aria-hidden="true">3</span>
    </figure>
    <ol class="ds-anatomy__list">
      <li><div><b>Leading icon (optional)</b><small>1.25em square, inherits the label colour, <code>aria-hidden="true"</code>.</small></div></li>
      <li><div><b>Label</b><small>A verb phrase in sentence case; it is the accessible name.</small></div></li>
      <li><div><b>Container</b><small>Height from <code>--control-height-*</code>, <code>--radius-md</code> corners, 1px border, horizontal padding <code>--space-3/4/6</code>.</small></div></li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="variants"><h2><a href="#variants">Variants</a></h2>
  <p>Variants change emphasis, not meaning. Pick by how much attention the action deserves on this view, then check there is still only one primary.</p>
  {{example:Emphasis from highest to lowest; danger is reserved for destructive confirmations.}}
<button class="btn btn--primary" type="button">Send request</button>
<button class="btn" type="button">Find braiders</button>
<button class="btn btn--ghost" type="button">Edit details</button>
<button class="btn btn--link" type="button">Cancel request</button>
<button class="btn btn--danger" type="button">Cancel appointment</button>
  {{/example}}
  <h3>With icons, icon-only and block</h3>
  {{example:Icon-only buttons carry <code>aria-label</code> and a tooltip; the icon itself is <code>aria-hidden</code>.}}
<button class="btn btn--primary" type="button">{{icon:calendar}}Request with Nia</button>
<button class="btn" type="button">Filters{{icon:filter}}</button>
<button class="btn btn--icon" type="button" aria-label="Edit request">{{icon:edit}}</button>
<button class="btn btn--ghost btn--icon" type="button" aria-label="Close dialog">{{icon:close}}</button>
<button class="btn btn--primary btn--block" type="button">Send request</button>
  {{/example}}
  <h3>As a link</h3>
  <p>Navigation that should look like an action, such as "See braiders for this style", uses <code>&lt;a class="btn"&gt;</code>. It keeps link semantics: it goes somewhere, opens with a middle click, and is announced as a link.</p>
  {{example:Same classes on <code>&lt;a href&gt;</code>; no <code>type</code> and no <code>disabled</code>.}}
<a class="btn btn--primary" href="../../mocks/pages/matching-braiders/default.html">See braiders for this style</a>
<a class="btn" href="../../mocks/pages/style-gallery/default.html">Explore styles</a>
  {{/example}}
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="sizes"><h2><a href="#sizes">Sizes</a></h2>
  <p>Medium is the default. Small lives in rows, toolbars and pagination; large is for hero and auth screens where the button is the whole point.</p>
  {{example:Heights <code>--control-height-sm/md/lg</code> (32/40/48px); padding <code>--space-3/4/6</code>; label <code>--font-size-sm/md/lg</code>.}}
<button class="btn btn--primary btn--sm" type="button">Small · 32px</button>
<button class="btn btn--primary" type="button">Medium · 40px</button>
<button class="btn btn--primary btn--lg" type="button">Large · 48px</button>
  {{/example}}
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="states"><h2><a href="#states">States</a></h2>
  <p>Every variant has the same six states. Pointer and focus states are forced here with <code>data-state</code> so they can be reviewed without a mouse; real pages get them from <code>:hover</code>, <code>:focus-visible</code>, <code>:active</code>, <code>:disabled</code> and <code>aria-busy</code>.</p>
  <div class="ds-matrix"><table>
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Variant</th><th scope="col">Default</th><th scope="col">Hover</th><th scope="col">Focus</th><th scope="col">Active</th><th scope="col">Disabled</th><th scope="col">Loading</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><th scope="row">Primary</th><td><button class="btn btn--primary" type="button">Send</button></td><td><button class="btn btn--primary" type="button" data-state="hover">Send</button></td><td><button class="btn btn--primary" type="button" data-state="focus">Send</button></td><td><button class="btn btn--primary" type="button" data-state="active">Send</button></td><td><button class="btn btn--primary" type="button" disabled>Send</button></td><td><button class="btn btn--primary" type="button" aria-busy="true">Send</button></td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Secondary</th><td><button class="btn" type="button">Filters</button></td><td><button class="btn" type="button" data-state="hover">Filters</button></td><td><button class="btn" type="button" data-state="focus">Filters</button></td><td><button class="btn" type="button" data-state="active">Filters</button></td><td><button class="btn" type="button" disabled>Filters</button></td><td><button class="btn" type="button" aria-busy="true">Filters</button></td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Ghost</th><td><button class="btn btn--ghost" type="button">Edit</button></td><td><button class="btn btn--ghost" type="button" data-state="hover">Edit</button></td><td><button class="btn btn--ghost" type="button" data-state="focus">Edit</button></td><td><button class="btn btn--ghost" type="button" data-state="active">Edit</button></td><td><button class="btn btn--ghost" type="button" disabled>Edit</button></td><td><button class="btn btn--ghost" type="button" aria-busy="true">Edit</button></td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Link</th><td><button class="btn btn--link" type="button">Cancel request</button></td><td><button class="btn btn--link" type="button" data-state="hover">Cancel request</button></td><td><button class="btn btn--link" type="button" data-state="focus">Cancel request</button></td><td><button class="btn btn--link" type="button" data-state="active">Cancel request</button></td><td><button class="btn btn--link" type="button" disabled>Cancel request</button></td><td><button class="btn btn--link" type="button" aria-busy="true">Cancel request</button></td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Danger</th><td><button class="btn btn--danger" type="button">Sign out</button></td><td><button class="btn btn--danger" type="button" data-state="hover">Sign out</button></td><td><button class="btn btn--danger" type="button" data-state="focus">Sign out</button></td><td><button class="btn btn--danger" type="button" data-state="active">Sign out</button></td><td><button class="btn btn--danger" type="button" disabled>Sign out</button></td><td><button class="btn btn--danger" type="button" aria-busy="true">Sign out</button></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
  <h3>Pressed (toggle)</h3>
  {{example:<code>aria-pressed="true"</code> uses the selected look shared with chips and the current nav link.}}
<button class="btn" type="button" aria-pressed="true">Saved</button>
<button class="btn" type="button" aria-pressed="false">Save braider</button>
  {{/example}}
  <h3>Both themes</h3>
  {{themes}}<button class="btn btn--primary" type="button">Send request</button><button class="btn" type="button">Filters</button><button class="btn btn--ghost" type="button">Edit</button><button class="btn btn--link" type="button">Cancel request</button><button class="btn btn--danger" type="button">Sign out</button>{{/themes}}
  <ul>
    <li><b>Loading</b> keeps the button's width and label (for its accessible name), paints the label transparent, shows a spinner, sets <code>aria-busy="true"</code> and ignores further clicks. Progress text ("Sending your request…") goes to the form's live region.</li>
    <li><b>Disabled</b> uses the native attribute; it is not focusable and is 50% opaque. Prefer leaving a button enabled and explaining the problem on activation; the offline booking form, for example, keeps "Send request" enabled and answers with the offline banner.</li>
    <li><b>Pressed</b> uses <code>aria-pressed</code> for a two-state toggle; the label stays the same or the change is announced.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="responsive"><h2><a href="#responsive">Responsive behaviour</a></h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Below <code>--layout-breakpoint-md</code> (768px) the primary action in a page header or form becomes full width; secondary actions follow beneath it (<code>.form-actions</code>, <code>.page-header__actions</code> do this for you).</li>
    <li>In dialog footers, buttons share the row and wrap with the primary first in reading order on phones (<code>flex-wrap: wrap-reverse</code>) and last (rightmost) from 640px.</li>
    <li>Medium (40px) and large (48px) buttons meet the 24px minimum target; on phones the primary action of a screen is large or full width so it reaches 44px.</li>
    <li>Labels never truncate or wrap. If a label wraps at 360px, shorten the verb phrase.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="theming"><h2><a href="#theming">Theming</a></h2>
  <p>The button reads only semantic tokens, mapped into component tokens (<code>--btn-bg</code>, <code>--btn-fg</code>, <code>--btn-border</code>, <code>--btn-bg-hover</code>, <code>--btn-bg-active</code>, <code>--btn-height</code>, <code>--btn-padding</code>, <code>--btn-font-size</code>) that each variant and size overrides. A theme changes semantic tokens; a one-off re-skin overrides component tokens; neither edits the rules.</p>
  <pre><code>/* A promotional banner with an inverse primary button */
.promo .btn--primary { --btn-bg: var(--color-bg-surface); --btn-fg: var(--color-fg-accent); --btn-border: var(--color-bg-surface); }</code></pre>
  <p>In the dark theme the accent lightens to plum 300 and the label flips to plum 950, so the pair stays above 7:1; danger does the same with the red ramp (red 300 with red 950 text).</p>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="accessibility"><h2><a href="#accessibility">Accessibility</a></h2>
  <h3>Role and pattern</h3>
  <p>Native <code>&lt;button type="button"&gt;</code>, or <code>type="submit"</code> inside a form; see the <a href="https://www.w3.org/WAI/ARIA/apg/patterns/button/">APG Button pattern</a>. A link styled as a button stays an <code>&lt;a href&gt;</code>; never a <code>&lt;div&gt;</code> with a click handler.</p>
  <h3>Keyboard</h3>
  <table class="ds-table ds-keys"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Key</th><th scope="col">Action</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><td><kbd>Tab</kbd> / <kbd>Shift</kbd>+<kbd>Tab</kbd></td><td>Moves focus to and from the button in DOM order.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><kbd>Enter</kbd></td><td>Activates a button or follows a button-styled link.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><kbd>Space</kbd></td><td>Activates a <code>&lt;button&gt;</code> on key up (not a link).</td></tr>
  </tbody></table>
  <h3>Focus</h3>
  <p>The shared ring (2px <code>--color-focus-ring</code>, 2px offset) appears on <code>:focus-visible</code> only. The offset gap shows the surface, so the ring stays at least 3:1 against both the plum button and the page. A loading button keeps focus.</p>
  <h3>Labelling</h3>
  <p>The visible label is the accessible name. Icon-only buttons set <code>aria-label</code> with a verb and object ("Close dialog", "Edit request") and show a tooltip on hover and focus. Do not change the label while loading; announce progress through a live region.</p>
  <h3>Contrast</h3>
  <div class="ds-example__canvas ds-example__canvas--stack" style="padding: 0; gap: var(--space-2);">
    {{pair:Label on primary|--color-fg-on-accent|--color-accent|4.5}}
    {{pair:Label on primary, hover|--color-fg-on-accent|--color-accent-hover|4.5}}
    {{pair:Label on danger|--color-fg-on-danger|--color-danger-solid|4.5}}
    {{pair:Secondary border on surface|--color-border-strong|--color-bg-surface|3}}
    {{pair:Focus ring on page|--color-focus-ring|--color-bg-canvas|3}}
  </div>
  <h3>Motion</h3>
  <p>Background, border and shadow transition over <code>--duration-fast</code> (120ms); the active state moves down 1px. Reduced motion zeroes the duration in the tokens. The loading spinner keeps turning because it is the only sign that work is in progress.</p>
  <h3>Touch</h3>
  <p>Medium and large buttons exceed the 24px minimum; a screen's primary mobile action is at least 44px tall. Small buttons (32px) only appear where neighbours are at least 8px apart.</p>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="content"><h2><a href="#content">Content</a></h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Labels are verb phrases in sentence case: "Send request", "Request a change", "Post review". Never "OK", "Submit", "Yes" or "Click here".</li>
    <li>Name the object when context does not: "Cancel request" in the dialog footer, not "Cancel".</li>
    <li>Pair a destructive action with a safe one that says what staying means: "Keep browsing" beside "Cancel request".</li>
    <li>Keep labels to three or four words. Use the braider's first name when it adds confidence: "Request with Nia".</li>
    <li>Do not swap the label for "Working…" while loading; the spinner and live region carry progress.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="do-dont"><h2><a href="#do-dont">Do and don't</a></h2>
  <div class="ds-dodont">
    <figure class="ds-do"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><button class="btn" type="button">Keep browsing</button><button class="btn btn--danger" type="button">Cancel request</button></div><figcaption>One emphasised action, placed last, with a safe action that says what staying means.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="ds-dont"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><button class="btn btn--primary" type="button">Try again</button><button class="btn btn--primary" type="button">Explore styles</button></div><figcaption>Two primary buttons compete. Make the recovery action primary and the other secondary.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="ds-do"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><button class="btn btn--ghost btn--icon" type="button" aria-label="Close dialog">{{icon:close}}</button></div><figcaption>Icon-only buttons use an SVG icon and an <code>aria-label</code>.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="ds-dont"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><button class="btn btn--primary" type="button" disabled>Working…</button></div><figcaption>Disable the button and replace its label while sending (as the mocks' submitting states do). Keep the label, set <code>aria-busy</code>, keep focus.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="tokens"><h2><a href="#tokens">Tokens</a></h2>
  <div class="ds-table-wrap"><table class="ds-table">
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Part</th><th scope="col">Token</th><th scope="col">Light</th><th scope="col">Dark</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      {{tok:Primary background|--color-accent}}
      {{tok:Primary background, hover|--color-accent-hover}}
      {{tok:Primary background, active|--color-accent-active}}
      {{tok:Primary label|--color-fg-on-accent}}
      {{tok:Secondary border|--color-border-strong}}
      {{tok:Secondary hover background|--color-bg-subtle}}
      {{tok:Danger background|--color-danger-solid}}
      {{tok:Danger label|--color-fg-on-danger}}
      {{tok:Link label|--color-fg-link}}
      {{tok:Focus ring|--color-focus-ring}}
      {{tok:Height sm / md / lg|--control-height-sm|--control-height-md|--control-height-lg}}
      {{tok:Padding sm / md / lg|--space-3|--space-4|--space-6}}
      {{tok:Radius|--radius-md}}
      {{tok:Label font|--text-label}}
      {{tok:Transition|--duration-fast|--ease-standard}}
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="code"><h2><a href="#code">Code</a></h2>
  <pre><code>&lt;button class="btn btn--primary" type="submit"&gt;Send request&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;button class="btn btn--primary" type="submit" aria-busy="true"&gt;Send request&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;a class="btn" href="/styles/knotless-braids/braiders"&gt;Find braiders&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;button class="btn btn--ghost btn--icon" type="button" aria-label="Close dialog"&gt;
  &lt;svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24"&gt;…&lt;/svg&gt;
&lt;/button&gt;</code></pre>
  <table class="ds-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Class / attribute</th><th scope="col">Effect</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><td><code>.btn</code></td><td>Base: secondary look, medium size.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>.btn--primary</code> <code>.btn--ghost</code> <code>.btn--link</code> <code>.btn--danger</code></td><td>Variant.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>.btn--sm</code> <code>.btn--lg</code></td><td>Size; omit for medium.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>.btn--icon</code></td><td>Square icon-only button; requires <code>aria-label</code>.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>.btn--block</code></td><td>Full width.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>disabled</code> / <code>aria-disabled="true"</code></td><td>Disabled look; the native attribute also removes it from the tab order.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>aria-busy="true"</code></td><td>Loading: spinner, label kept but painted transparent, clicks ignored, width kept.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>aria-pressed</code></td><td>Toggle state.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>data-state="hover|focus|active|loading|pressed"</code></td><td>Documentation and mocks only: forces a state in a static page.</td></tr>
  </tbody></table>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="sources"><h2><a href="#sources">Sources</a></h2>
  <p>Extracted from these mocks:</p>
  <ul>
    {{mock:pages/style-gallery/default|secondary "Find braiders" beside search}}
    {{mock:pages/booking-request/default|primary submit}}
    {{mock:pages/booking-request/submitting|busy submit}}
    {{mock:pages/appointment-detail/default|secondary and link actions on the appointment card}}
    {{mock:dialogs/cancel-appointment/default|danger confirm, ghost icon close}}
    {{mock:pages/style-gallery/error|primary recovery with secondary alternative}}
  </ul>
  <p>Drift fixed during extraction: busy buttons were also <code>disabled</code> and relabelled "Working…" (system keeps the label, sets only <code>aria-busy</code>, keeps focus); the dialog close button used a "×" text glyph (system uses the close icon); the spinner was 1.1em, off the icon size (now 1.25em).</p>
</section>
